- `action(n1, "start the process")`: Hallucinates an initial step; the source begins directly with "reviewing the received application."
- `action(n12, "end the process")`: Hallucinates a terminal step; the source simply states "the process will come to an end."
- `branch(b1, XOR)` and `branch(b2, XOR)`: Missing `guard` statements on outgoing edges (`b1,n6`, `b1,n7`, `b2,n9`, `b2,n10`) to enforce the source's conditional routing: "If the answer is yes... if the answer is no."
- `defines(v1, "are there any new findings", {})` and `defines(v2, "are there any new findings", {})`: Specifies empty ranges `{}` instead of a binary domain (e.g., `{true, false}` or `{"yes", "no"}`) required by the source's yes/no evaluation.
- `actor(a_default, "Default", [...])`: Labels the participant "Default" instead of the source-identified responsible party, the "review clerk."
- `action(n5, "are there any new findings")` and `action(n8, "are there any new findings")`: Misrepresents a decision predicate as a process action; the source treats it as a conditional check that directly drives exclusive choices ("check if there are any new findings. If the answer is yes...").

Structural Check
- [S1] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v2` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S2] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n6` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n7` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n9` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n10` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.